## Bundled third-party work

magpie ships the following inside the extension package. Each keeps its own
licence; the MIT grant above covers magpie's own code only.

**Readability.js** — Mozilla, Mozilla Public License 2.0.
<https://github.com/mozilla/readability>

**pdf.js** — Mozilla, Apache License 2.0.
<https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js>

**WebLLM** — MLC AI, Apache License 2.0. <https://github.com/mlc-ai/web-llm>

**Compiled model libraries** (`src/vendor/wasm/*.wasm`) — MLC AI, Apache License
2.0, from <https://github.com/mlc-ai/binary-mlc-llm-libs>. Vendored rather than
fetched at runtime because Chrome treats a remotely-fetched `.wasm` as
remotely-hosted code, which the Web Store rejects.

**Space Grotesk** — Florian Karsten, SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence text at
`src/fonts/OFL-Space-Grotesk.txt`.

**JetBrains Mono** — JetBrains, SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence text at
`src/fonts/OFL-JetBrains-Mono.txt`.

Model *weights* are not bundled. They are downloaded once from Hugging Face and
cached by the browser, and each carries the licence of its own model — Qwen2.5,
Llama 3.2 and Gemma 3 respectively.
